    "sourceAuthor": "MD Live Help Center",
    "body": "# MD Live Service Basics\n\nMD Live offers 24/7 health care by phone or video through a national network of board-certified doctors, pediatricians, dermatologists, psychiatrists, and therapists — covering hundreds of medical and mental health needs with no surprise costs.\n\n## Availability\n\nUrgent care doctors are available 24/7/365 for on-demand visits. Scheduled appointments — therapy, primary care — depend on provider availability, though evenings and weekends are typically open for all services.\n\n## Cost\n\nCreating an account is free. With a health plan or employer benefit, visits can cost as little as $0; you're only charged after scheduling and confirming payment. MD Live accepts most major credit and debit cards.\n\n## Privacy\n\nConfidentiality is part of MD Live's Code of Ethics, and HIPAA protects personal health information. Info is shared with a patient's primary care provider only in accordance with applicable law.\n\n## Getting started\n\nCreate a free account, then fill out a medical history profile so your provider is prepared for the first appointment. Card details are only requested when you actually book care.\n\n## Related Concepts\n\n- [[Dermatology Acne Treatment]] — dermatology care available through the same service\n- [[Insurance Coverage Basics]] — how cost and coverage work per visit\n- [[Men's Health Prescriptions]] — prescription-based care through MD Live\n- [[Mental Health Appointments & Provider Selection]] — scheduling therapy and psychiatry\n- [[Pediatric Care Vaccines & Wellness]] — pediatric service coverage"
