    "sourceAuthor": "MD Live Help Center",
    "body": "# Dermatology Acne Treatment\n\nBoard-certified dermatologists on MD Live treat hormonal, bacterial, and cystic acne over video or phone, using submitted photos in place of an in-person skin exam.\n\n## Diagnosis by photo\n\nPatients send clear photos of affected areas from multiple angles; the dermatologist assesses type and severity before recommending treatment.\n\n## Treatment options\n\nOptions include topical creams (benzoyl peroxide, retinoids, antibiotics), oral medications (antibiotics, hormonal treatments, isotretinoin), and general skincare guidance.\n\n## Isotretinoin (Accutane)\n\nIsotretinoin needs close monitoring and baseline labs that require an in-person visit. MD Live dermatologists can evaluate candidacy and refer patients to a local dermatologist when appropriate.\n\n## Timeline\n\nTopical treatments typically show results in 4-8 weeks; oral medications take 8-12 weeks. Consistency matters more than speed.\n\n## Cost\n\nMany acne treatments are covered by insurance, and generic options are often available — MD Live can estimate out-of-pocket cost before treatment starts.\n\n## Related Concepts\n\n- [[MD Live Service Basics]] — how telehealth visits work in general"
