    "sourceUrl": "https://github.com/kriziaf/help-center-chat/blob/main/public/insurance/insurance-coverage-basics.md",
    "sourceAuthor": "MD Live Help Center",
    "body": "# Insurance Coverage Basics\n\nMD Live accepts most major insurance plans — Aetna, Anthem, Blue Cross/Blue Shield, Cigna, Humana, UnitedHealthcare, and others — with coverage confirmed during signup.\n\n## Checking coverage\n\nEntering insurance details at signup shows the exact copay, or confirms a visit is covered at no cost, before any appointment is booked.\n\n## Typical copays\n\nCopays range from $0 to $50+ depending on plan, and some plans cover telehealth visits completely. Pricing is always shown upfront.\n\n## Paying without insurance\n\nUninsured patients pay out-of-pocket, typically $59-$99 per visit depending on visit type, with payment plans sometimes available.\n\n## HSA / FSA\n\nMost Health Savings Accounts and Flexible Spending Accounts cover MD Live visits — check with the account administrator for specifics.\n\n## Claims and appeals\n\nMD Live handles insurance claims processing and can help file an appeal if a claim is denied; keep visit receipts and explanation-of-benefits documents.\n\n## Related Concepts\n\n- [[MD Live Service Basics]] — how visits and billing fit together"
