    "sourceAuthor": "MD Live Help Center",
    "body": "# Men's Health Prescriptions\n\nMD Live doctors can prescribe and manage common men's health treatments, from hair loss to hormone therapy, without an in-person visit for most cases.\n\n## Hair loss\n\nFinasteride (Propecia) can be prescribed for male pattern baldness when appropriate — it works best started early and taken consistently. Minoxidil (Rogaine), a topical treatment, can be prescribed alone or combined with finasteride for better results.\n\n## Testosterone replacement therapy\n\nDoctors evaluate symptoms of low testosterone and, if appropriate, prescribe TRT via injections, gels, patches, or pellets, with regular monitoring required.\n\n## Refills\n\nRefills can be requested through the MD Live app or portal; for ongoing treatments, a doctor may set up automatic renewals sent directly to a pharmacy.\n\n## Cost\n\nCoverage varies by plan — MD Live can clarify coverage before prescribing, and many treatments have covered generic alternatives.\n\n## Related Concepts\n\n- [[MD Live Service Basics]] — how prescriptions fit into a typical visit"
