    "sourceAuthor": "MD Live Help Center",
    "body": "# Pediatric Care Vaccines & Wellness\n\nMD Live pediatricians support childhood wellness and vaccination needs through video visits, coordinating with local providers when an in-person step is required.\n\n## Vaccinations\n\nPediatricians evaluate vaccine needs against CDC guidelines (DTaP, MMR, polio, hepatitis, and others) and can provide prescriptions or referrals to local pediatricians or pharmacies — some vaccines must still be given in person.\n\n## Well-child visits\n\nTelehealth well-child visits cover growth, development, nutrition, and parenting questions; a complete physical exam may need an in-person follow-up.\n\n## School and sports physicals\n\nSome wellness visits can happen over telehealth, but sports physicals often require an in-person exam and signature — MD Live can confirm which applies.\n\n## Developmental screening\n\nPediatricians screen for developmental concerns by reviewing milestones like speech, motor skills, and social development; more extensive evaluation may need an in-person specialist.\n\n## Preventive care\n\nServices include developmental screening, nutrition counseling, behavior guidance, and exercise/screen-time recommendations to catch issues early.\n\n## Related Concepts\n\n- [[MD Live Service Basics]] — how pediatric visits fit into the overall service"
